config: compute the USE of an ebuild Package without setcpv()

Sub-series: A (probe, match and config memos) - patch 8 of 10; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Of these it needs 0012 only.
Ported to upstream 73646c35d: adapted: upstream 64701b0a3 repaired the chained comparison in setcpv(), so setcpv() no longer always reaches reset(): the validity text in _pkg_use_fast() is rewritten for that (an early return leaves no template, the next package takes setcpv()); _pkg_use_fast() returns None for a package with cycle_use_changes (--cycle-break, 238ae9ad8), whose forced flags setcpv() adds to USE; last hunk: context (_read_pkg_env)

Creating a Package for an ebuild called setcpv() only to read five values
back: PORTAGE_USE, USE_EXPAND, USE_EXPAND_HIDDEN, useforce and usemask.
config._pkg_use_fast(pkg) computes the same five values without setcpv():
setcpv() always calls reset(), so its result for a package depends on the
previous package only through package.env, repository make.defaults and
FEATURES=test. At the end of a complete setcpv() a template of the constant
stacking inputs is recorded (not in any of those three cases) and
modifying() drops it. With a template, only the USE strings of the "pkg",
"defaults" and "pkginternal" dicts differ per package; they are computed
with the statements of setcpv() and stacked with the same
_regenerate_use_stack and memo as regenerate(). The method returns None,
and the caller runs setcpv() as before, for built packages, packages with
package.env or repository settings, "+flag" tokens and "_*" wildcards.

On top of patches 0001-0015, resolve seconds before -> after
(median of the runs, at least 2 per figure):
  start 34.2 -> 32.3, holds 18.0 -> 16.0, masks 36.9 -> 34.7,
  py313 21.5 -> 19.4, bdeps 25.4 -> 23.2, policykit 18.4 -> 16.5
  sum of six 154.4 -> 142.1 (-12.3 s, -2.7 % of the stock sum 447.5)
Patches 0001-0016 together: 447.5 -> 142.1 s (-68 %); 447.5 is the
stock sum of the ladder run of 2026-11-20, stock was not run again here.

Weak spots and what was not checked:
* Not a proof for every configuration: it rests on the analysis that
  setcpv() results depend on the previous package only via package.env, repo
  make.defaults and FEATURES=test. The template is dropped by
  config.modifying(); code that edits the dicts of doebuild_settings
  directly would not invalidate it. After resolution doebuild_settings holds
  the state of the last real setcpv(). The built-in self-test hook
  (_PKG_USE_FAST_SELFTEST) was not run for this series.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
